  "seoBody": "<h2>What quarry inspection software is for</h2><p>Quarries and mines make a lot of records. Plant checks. Tip and tailings lagoon inspections. Site safety audits. Each must be accurate, dated and complete. Software does not make an inspection valid. You do.</p><h2>The rules</h2><p>Quarries in Great Britain come under the Quarries Regulations 1999. Mines come under the Mines Regulations 2014. Both sit under the Health and Safety at Work etc. Act 1974. The HSE enforces. This is not legal advice. Check the current rules and your site rules.</p><h2>Three duties</h2><h3>1. Plant</h3><p>Excavators, dump trucks, crushers, screens and conveyors come under PUWER 1998. Lifting equipment comes under LOLER 1998. Take a photo for each item.</p><h3>2. Tips and tailings lagoons</h3><p>These carry inspection duties. An appointed specialist makes the geotechnical assessment. Your record shows what you saw, where and when.</p><h3>3. Site safety audit</h3><p>An audit against the Quarries Regulations 1999 covers vehicle and pedestrian segregation, edge protection, dust, signs and welfare.</p><h2>Dust and silica</h2><p>Quarrying makes respirable crystalline silica. It is a serious health hazard, controlled under COSHH. Quickler can record that controls were in place, with photos. It does not measure exposure. Check the current HSE guidance.</p><h2>What to look for in the software</h2><ul><li><strong>Record on site:</strong> not afterwards</li><li><strong>A photo for each fault:</strong> faults are listed with their place</li><li><strong>A clean report:</strong> Word, PDF or a web link</li><li><strong>No charge per seat:</strong> Quickler is £75 per month per phone number & unlimited free dashboard accounts. Everyone else is free</li></ul><p><strong>Please note:</strong> Quickler records the evidence and writes the report. It does not replace you as the competent person. A tip assessment still needs the appointed specialist. <a href=\"/pages/help/index.html#contact-form-section\">Ask us</a> if that matters for your work.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What is quarry inspection software?</h3><p>It is a tool that helps you record an inspection and write the report. That means plant checks, tip and tailings inspections and safety audits. You can use paper, an audit app like iAuditor, or Quickler in WhatsApp.</p><h3>What regulations govern quarry and mine inspections in the UK?</h3><p>Quarries in Great Britain come under the Quarries Regulations 1999. Mines come under the Mines Regulations 2014. Plant comes under PUWER 1998 and LOLER 1998. The HSE is the regulator. This is not legal advice.</p><h3>Can I run quarry inspections over WhatsApp?</h3><p>Yes. Quickler asks the questions in WhatsApp. You answer by text, voice note or photo. When you say done, Quickler writes the report. No new app and no login.</p><h3>Does the software replace the competent person or geotechnical specialist?</h3><p>No. Quickler records the evidence and writes the report. A tip assessment still needs the appointed specialist. You make the judgement.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/quarry-plant-inspection-checklist-uk.html\">Quarry plant inspection checklist</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/tip-tailings-inspection-report-uk.html\">Tip and tailings inspection reports</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/mines-quarries-safety-audit-uk.html\">Mines and quarries safety audit</a></li></ul>",
